ex v via pebbling moves. The Target Conjecture states that π(G, D) ≤ π_|D|(G) for every target distribution D, where |D| = ∑_v D(v). We introduce and provide evidence for a new Strong Target Conjecture: π(G, D) ≤ π_|D|(G) − s(D)(|D| − 1), where s(D) is the number of vertices s.t. D(v) > 0.\n\nLiliana Alcon  \nUniversidad Nacional De La Plata - CONICET  \nliliana.alcon.unlp@gmail.com\n\nGlenn Hurlbert  \nVirginia Commonwealth University  \nghurlbert@vcu.edu\n\nMS18  \nOptimal Pebbling Number of the Square Grid\n\nA pebbling move on a graph removes two pebbles from a vertex and adds one pebble to an adjacent vertex. A vertex is reachable from a pebble distribution if it is possible to move a pebble to that vertex using pebbling moves. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nG. Hurlbert Publications (https://glennhurlbert.github.io/pubs.html)\nciteturn7search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago;  | 94    | On the strong target conjecture for Kneser graphs (with V. ...  | 78    | On the target pebbling conjecture (with E. Seddiq), Combinatorics, Graph Theory and Computing, Springer Proc. ... Hurlbert), in G4G12 Exchange Book (v. ... [This paper won the Best Undergraduate Research Award from the Mathematical Association of America in 2004.]\n | 98    | Pebbling in $k$-paths (with L. Alcón), in preparation.\n | 97    | On EKR and HK trees (with E. Estrugo, V. Kamat, and A. Pastine), in preparation.\n | 96    | Graham's conjecture for Petersen graph powers, in preparation.\n | 95    | Optimal pebbling density of grid strips (with Z. Hefty and C. Muir), in preparation.\n | 94    | On the strong target conjecture for Kneser graphs (with V. Bardenova), in preparation.\n | 93    | Pebbling in diameter 3 Johnson graphs (with P. Fay), in preparation.\n | 92    | Target pebbling in grids (with M. Tennant), in preparation.\n | 91    | Closed neighborhood balanced coloring of chordal graphs (with A. Trenk), in preparation.\n | 90    | 